            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0850" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg714"/>

                <head>No. 518.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 4, 1888</date>.
                        (Received May 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 742 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >bis</hi>).]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith for
                    your information a copy of a question asked in the House of Commons on Thursday,
                    the 3d instant, in regard to affairs of Samoa, and also a copy of the answer
                    made by Sir James Fergusson, the under secretary of state for foreign
                    affairs.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d518-a1.xml" xpointer="d518-a1"/>
            </div>
